{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791594542,"nonce":"/zb3zi1RtfTxTh6aSIgWPVFE9iw=","message":"Found while checking what CSS the host applies (2026-10-10): transition and animation declarations are accepted by the cascade and then dropped. @keyframes compile, but compileCss().keyframes returns names only, so nothing can play them.\n\nReference, for structure, from a survey of ashui (not re-run here): haxe/ashui/css/CssMotion.hx and Animations.hx, and animation/{Transition,Tweened,Spring,SpringConfig,AnimatedValue,LayoutAnimation,AnimationScheduler}.hx. It has a tick scheduler that sleeps until the next timer, a property interpolator by type (colour, length, transform, shadow, filter), transition and animation driven from the cascade, a [closing] attribute with whenPlayed for exit animations, an RK4 spring, and FLIP with children clipped during a resize. Its component sheet leans on about 27 transitions and 15 keyframe blocks.\n\nNeeds on the engine side: expose keyframe steps (blinc_abi css/mod.rs keyframes_named) and a per-frame hook on NativeWindowHost. set_visual and sized-visual clipping already exist. The user-agent sheet and a Base UI-style adapter are waiting on this for popup and state transitions.","files":null}]}